B.G2=new A.V(17,"Make them answer you",B.a1,"A move that forces a reply keeps the initiative. If you spend the game responding to them, you only need to be wrong once. Here one move takes the game away from them entirely.",B.af,B.K0,4,null,B.l,"Column 5 leaves two squares that each finish a four for the amber sunbursts. Initiative is not aggression; it is being the side that decides what the position is about. A fork is simply the strongest form of it.",!0,B.i,null,null)
